  "_comment": "EXP-1057 / SLOP-16: THE mini-graph look, identical x4 (web lib/issue-graph.ts, desktop domain::issue_graph, iOS ExpCore IssueGraph.Geometry, Android domain/IssueGraph.Geometry). Points (web px = desktop px = iOS pt = Android dp). The graph is VERTICAL: waves are ROWS (top = the first blockers, bottom = the blocked subject), lanes are COLUMNS. A node box sits at x = inset + lane * (nodeWidth + laneGap), y = inset + wave * (nodeHeight + waveGap); the grid is the boxes plus `inset` on every side (room for the rings, never clipped). The viewport is min(grid, maxView*) and scrolls past it; a chain never scrolls sideways. An edge leaves its blocker's bottom-middle and enters the blocked box's top-middle; forward it curves inside the gap, both control points on the gap's middle (c1 = start + bend down, c2 = end - bend up); a backward (cycle) edge bows by max(waveGap / 2, |dy| / 2). The HOVER graphs (rail popover, the Related work view) draw the SMALL chip in `compactNodeWidth` boxes; the blocked-start dialogs keep `nodeWidth`. Every origin/size/edge rule takes the node width as an override, and the `compact` cases are the same rules at that width. The rail (web + desktop lists) draws DOTS only: `railGutter` + `railNodeWidth` wide, a `railDot` dot with a `railDotRing` ring; hovering a dot opens the mini-graph.",
